                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.24011/2611.24011v1/transfer.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Stage 1: Cross-Morphology Policy Adaptation and Acceleration.Stage 1.1 (Sec.3.1.1) fine-tunes an arm-centric WAM on quadruped demonstrations synthesized in QLM-Bench (Sec.4).\nVisual Adaptation replaces the head and wrist views (images from Mobile ALOHA[13]) by the ego-centric and top-down views, Action Adaptation replaces the 30-dimensional arm command by the 9-dimensional quadruped command, and the whole-body controller𝒞\\mathcal{C}converts each command into joint torques.\nStage 1.2, OPSD (Sec.3.1.2), distills the transferred policy, as the high-NFE teacherπT\\pi_{\\mathrm{T}}, into the 1/2-NFE studentπS\\pi_{\\mathrm{S}}; the generation time counts the sampling of video and action only.\nBottom right shows the closed loop of the policy on the task “Press the button.”\nImagined views and rendered demonstrations are illustrations.",
                "position": 446
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.24011/2611.24011v1/opd.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:On-Policy Self-Distillation (Stage 1.2, top) and Stage 2 (bottom).Top left (Training Context): training contexts mix the teacher cache, which the frozen teacher collects in closed loop before training, with the contexts that the student reaches in its own streaming rollouts (H∼d¯H\\sim\\bar{d}).\nTop right (Target & Loss): on each context, teacher and student sample from the same noise, and the student’s one-step video stream and two-step action stream are regressed to the targets of the teacher’s high-NFE sampler, with a stop-gradient on the plan that conditions the student’s action.\nBottom: Stage 2.1 tunes the OPSD teacher by reinforcement learning into a specialist teacher for each selected task (Sec.3.2.1), and Stage 2.2, M-OPD, distills the teachers, routed by task, into one 1/2-NFE student that starts from the OPSD student (Sec.3.2.2).\nPlan images and rendered actions are illustrations, not model outputs.",
                "position": 470
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.24011/2611.24011v1/qlm_bench_tasks.png",
